    Document JSON logging.
    
    The central logging guide is where an operator is told how to turn log
    collection on and how to search what it gathers, so it is where the
    choice of log format belongs.
    
    The guide already tells people to search on Hostname, Payload and
    programname, so the important thing to state is that those keep
    working: the fields are the same in either format, and what JSON adds
    is the detail the text format throws away. The two constraints worth
    knowing in advance are also recorded -- that the setting covers every
    oslo.log service at once because they share one parser, and that
    services which do not use oslo.log, Horizon among them, ignore it.
    
    Prompt: Michael asked whether the series was complete. It was not:
    nothing documented the new option for operators, which is the first
    thing a reviewer would ask for.
    
