+Log format
+~~~~~~~~~~
+
+By default the OpenStack services write logs in oslo.log's text format,
+and Fluentd recovers the fields from them with a regular expression.
+Setting ``openstack_logging_json`` makes them emit JSON instead:
+
+.. code-block:: yaml
+
+   openstack_logging_json: true
+
+Fluentd reads either form and produces the same fields, so searches on
+``Hostname``, ``Payload``, ``programname`` and the rest are unaffected.
+What JSON adds is the detail the text format discards or flattens into
+the message: the request context arrives already structured rather than
+as a ``[req-... ]`` prefix to be taken apart again, timestamps keep
+their sub-second precision, and the source file, line number and
+function of each message are preserved.
+
+This is one setting for every oslo.log service rather than a per
+service one. All of them are read by a single Fluentd input, which has
+a single parser, so a service logging in a different format to its
+neighbours would not be collected at all.
+
+Services that do not use oslo.log, Horizon among them, do not honour
+this setting. They are unaffected because they do not write to the log
+files this input reads. If you have configured one of them to do so,
+its logs will no longer be parsed once this option is enabled.
+
